sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 + 5, single-swamp-node, swamp-role-includes-caddy, swamp-workers-two-concurrency. docs/cli/node.mdx#orbit-noderoleadd, docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#native-role-convergence.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:role:add
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>has the role
  participant M as Metrics Node<br/>Prometheus
  CLI->>GW: node:role:add 12 app-dev<br/>--converge
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:add 12 app-dev --converge`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> --converge [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node, by id or exact name, and a role it already has
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - applies the role's packages, files, units and publication again, and repairs drift
  %%> - never changes an Instance, a Process, a Schedule or the role assignment itself
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  %%> - `node:converge` runs the same role steps for each active role, but only for parts whose digest changed
  Note over GW: Validate, claim the role<br/>role: provisioning · task #5171
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node and has the `app-dev` role
  %%> - the role is `active`, `failed` at a `converge:` step, or `provisioning` with a stale claim: older than 11 minutes, with no operation holding the role lock
  %%> - the role is not `vpn` or `router`; `node:converge` re-applies the `vpn` files
  %%> - one role operation per Node: the Gateway waits up to 2 minutes for Node 12's role lock, then refuses with `node_role.node_busy`
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the complete role plan, with one digest per part
  %%> - the current Metrics fleet change for Node 12, when there is one
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the role marked provisioning, and task #5171 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-converge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the role plan with its files and digests, and the vault key names of the role credentials
  %%> - Node 12's and the Metrics Node's addresses and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5171
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Install prerequisites<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/apt · Tool Managers
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs only what is missing or below its pin; a package at its pin stays, so nothing restarts for it
  %%> - `app-dev`, `app-prod`: the shared Tool Manager setup step for `vp` and `composer`
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors (apt, fetch, file) over SSH from 209
  SW->>N: Apply the role runtime<br/>files, units · reload on change
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes each file of the role, and reloads a service only when one of its files changed
  %%> Per role:
  %%> - Caddy roles (`gateway`, `router`, `ingress`, `app-dev`, `app-prod`, `websocket`, `analytics`, `swamp`): Caddy package floor, the reload kernel setting, then the Caddyfile; validates it first and reloads Caddy gracefully
  %%> - `app-dev`, `app-prod`: the managed PHP-FPM module; validates each running master and reloads the valid ones gracefully
  %%> - `app-dev`: the `/etc/tmpfiles.d/orbit.conf` rule for `/tmp/orbit-*` and `/dev/shm/orbit-*`; restarts nothing
  %%> - `vpn`, through `node:converge`: the private DNS listener, records and catalog; restarts dnsmasq or the listener only for a change, and restores the last good copy when the new one fails its check
  %%> - `websocket`: the Reverb service
  %%> - `metrics`: the same steps as `metrics:enable`; a Prometheus config change is a reload
  %%> - `swamp`: Orbit's Caddy and the 2 worker services `orbit-swamp-worker@a` and `@b`
  %%> The swamp role's workers:
  %%> - this run runs on them, so converge never stops or removes them
  %%> - a changed worker unit takes effect at the worker's next restart
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors (file, systemd, docker) over SSH from 209
  opt certificate missing or due
    SW->>GW: Sign the role certificate<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
    %%> When:
    %%> - the role's Orbit certificate is missing, doesn't match its key, or is close to expiry
    %%> How:
    %%> - a step creates a new key on Node 12 and reads only the CSR; the Gateway signs it with the Orbit CA
    %%> - this is the one call a step may make to the Gateway
    GW-->>SW: Signed certificate<br/>leaf + chain
    %%> What happens next:
    %%> - Swamp writes the certificate beside its key on Node 12 and activates it
  end
  SW->>N: Publish and open ports<br/>Caddy, PHP, DNS · ufw
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - publishes the role's Caddy sites and PHP pools again, validated, with a graceful reload only on change
  %%> - applies the role's managed firewall rules; an existing identical line stays as it is
  %%> - re-publishes the role's private DNS names through the shared DNS step on the `vpn` Node
  opt Metrics fleet changed
    SW->>N: Converge the exporters<br/>node-exporter · cAdvisor
    %%> When:
    %%> - Node 12 is a selected exporter and its exporters or their firewall allows drifted
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the same steps as `metrics:exporter:enable`
    SW->>M: Publish the config<br/>validate, reload Prometheus
    %%> When:
    %%> - only when the Prometheus configuration changed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - validates it with `promtool`, publishes it, and reloads Prometheus while it runs
  end
  SW->>N: Check the role<br/>units active · files match
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the role's services are active and answer, such as Caddy, PHP-FPM or Reverb
  %%> - reads each applied file back and compares it with its digest
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the role only counts as converged when Node 12 shows it
  alt every step passes
    N-->>SW: role services ready
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed for every part of the role
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway for a result
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>role: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `app-dev` role on Node 12 is active again, with the digest of each applied part
    %%> - a failed step from an earlier run is cleared
    %%> - task #5171 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no match
    %%> When:
    %%> - a package, file, unit, Caddy validation, certificate, firewall or check step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the role failed<br/>converge:STEP · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the role is marked failed at `converge:STEP`, with the step's own error code
    %%> - task #5171 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback, except the DNS listener's restore of its last good copy
    %%> - running services keep their last valid configuration, because nothing reloads with one that fails validation
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause; it is a new task
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5171
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
